# Autonomous Ship / Pull

Follow `docs/AUTONOMOUS-GIT-OPERATIONS.md` (Asia/Taipei).

## When you are an Implementer

At Ship A (06:00) / Ship B (16:00), or when told to ship:

1. Commit unfinished work on **your** work branch (not `development`/`staging`/`main`).
2. Push the branch.
3. Open or update a PR targeting **`development`**.
4. Stop. Do not merge. Do not self-review. Bugbot reviews; Integrator merges.

At Pull A (08:00) / Pull B (18:00), or when told to pull:

1. Fetch and merge (or rebase only if already the repo rule) latest **`origin/development`** into your work branch.
2. Report blockers briefly; do not invent merges into `staging`/`main`.

## Hard stops

- Never merge your own PR into `development`.
- Never promote to `staging` or `main`.
- Never act as Reviewer on your own PR.
- After CI/Bugbot failure: expect a **Cloud Fix agent** (not you) unless you are that Fix agent.
- Fix agent: max **3** attempts on the same branch, then stop and leave `Issues`.

## Worktrees

Allowed. Prefer cleanup after merge/abandon. Caps: 12 worktrees / 20 GB (Cursor-managed).

## Status line (when Automations ask)

Write or update Lisa pipeline status as one of: `Ship A|Ship B|Pull A|Pull B: Clear|Issues` — no lists or links in that line.
